{"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/mutabledirectedgraph"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"relationshipsSections":[{"type":"inheritsFrom","title":"Inherits From","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/BidirectionalDirectedGraph","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph"],"kind":"relationships"}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"metadata":{"externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols015MutableDirectedA0P","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MutableDirectedGraph","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"MutableDirectedGraph","remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph.swift#L53","fileName":"MutableDirectedGraph.swift"},"fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MutableDirectedGraph","kind":"identifier"}],"modules":[{"name":"GraphProtocols"}],"symbolKind":"protocol","roleHeading":"Protocol","role":"symbol"},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols"]]},"abstract":[{"text":"A bidirectional directed graph that generic code can mutate: Boost’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MutableGraph"},{"text":" concept","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"add_vertex"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"add_edge"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"remove_edge"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"remove_vertex"},{"text":"), for a directed representation. It exists so that a wrapper which adds a rule, such as ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DirectedAcyclicGraph"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"can own any of the mutable representations as its base and still run at the base’s speed.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","topicSections":[{"anchor":"Initializers","title":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph\/init()"],"generated":true},{"anchor":"Instance-Methods","title":"Instance Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph\/insert(_:)","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph\/remove(_:)","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph\/remove(edge:)","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph\/removeAll(keepingCapacity:)","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph\/removeAllEdges(keepingCapacity:)","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph\/reserveCapacity(vertexCount:edgeCount:)"],"generated":true}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MutableDirectedGraph","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/Vertex","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P6VertexQa","text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"> : ","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/BidirectionalDirectedGraph","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols021BidirectionalDirectedA0P","text":"BidirectionalDirectedGraph","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/Vertices-swift.associatedtype","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P8VerticesQa","text":"Vertices","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa","text":"Index","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" == ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Keys.","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" Each vertex has a key: its index in ","type":"text"},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (","type":"text"},{"code":"Vertices.Index == Int","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"). On a dense","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"representation (","type":"text"},{"code":"AdjacencyList","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"DirectedPseudograph","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") the key is the vertex’s slot, which is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"also its ","type":"text"},{"code":"vertexIndex(of:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"; on ","type":"text"},{"code":"StableDirectedGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" it is the vertex’s position, which never","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"changes while the vertex exists and may leave holes. The underscored members read and write the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"graph by key, with no hashing, so a wrapper hashes a vertex once and then works on keys.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Laws."}]},{"text":" In addition to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BidirectionalDirectedGraph"},{"text":"’s:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"_key(of: v)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"code":"vertices.firstIndex(of: v)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and ","type":"text"},{"code":"_vertex(atKey:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is its inverse.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"For a vertex with key ","type":"text"},{"code":"k","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": ","type":"text"},{"code":"_successors(ofKey: k)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"_predecessors(ofKey: k)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"_outEdges(ofKey: k)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"_inEdges(ofKey: k)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"_outDegree(ofKey: k)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"_inDegree(ofKey: k)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"are the members of the same name without the label, for that vertex.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"_successorKeys(ofKey: k)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"_predecessorKeys(ofKey: k)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" are the far ends’ keys, in the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"same order; ","type":"text"},{"code":"_sourceKey(ofEdgeAt:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"_targetKey(ofEdgeAt:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" are the endpoints’ keys.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"_insertVertex(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" appends a vertex, which must not already be one, and returns its key:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"vertices.endIndex","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" before the call. Keys of other vertices do not change.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_insertEdge(fromKey:toKey:)"},{"type":"text","text":" inserts the edge and returns its position. On a simple graph"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AdjacencyList"},{"type":"text","text":"), an edge already present is not inserted again and its position is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"returned. Inserting an edge changes no key."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"_removeVertex(atKey: k)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" removes the vertex and every edge at it. If the representation fills","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the hole by moving another vertex in (a swap-remove), it returns that vertex’s old key, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the vertex’s key is now ","type":"text"},{"code":"k","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"; otherwise it returns ","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and no other key changes.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"_removeEdge(at:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" removes the edge at a live position and returns it, trapping on any other","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"position. Removing an edge changes no key.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"remove(v)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"code":"_removeVertex(atKey: _key(of: v)!)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", returning the removed instance.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_built(vertices:sourceKeys:targetKeys:reportingPositions:_:)"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"init()"},{"text":", then","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_insertVertex(_:)"},{"text":" for each vertex in order, then ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_insertEdge(fromKey:toKey:)"},{"text":" for each pair","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"in order: the same graph, and the same position for each pair.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Key density.","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" A wrapper may keep one table entry per 1024 keys, from the smallest live key"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices.endIndex"},{"type":"text","text":", plus O(1) per live vertex: the memory of the representation’s own page"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"table. On a dense representation the keys are "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0..<vertexCount"},{"type":"text","text":". On "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"StableDirectedGraph"},{"type":"text","text":" the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"span can exceed the vertex count: removals leave holes, and a decoded graph may start at any"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"position (its decoder bounds the span at "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"16 × vertexCount + 64"},{"type":"text","text":" pages). Keys before the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"smallest live key cost nothing."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Key rows.","type":"text"}]},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_successorKeys(ofKey:)"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_predecessorKeys(ofKey:)"},{"text":" return the stored rows","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"typed as ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SuccessorIndices"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PredecessorIndices"},{"text":", whose elements here are keys. On a dense","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"representation keys and indices coincide. On ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"StableDirectedGraph"},{"text":" the elements are positions,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"which are vertex indices only while the graph has no holes; ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"successorIndices(ofIndex:)"},{"text":" is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"then unavailable, but the key rows are not.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Not requirements."}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"insert(edge:)"},{"type":"text","text":" differs in its return type: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AdjacencyList"},{"type":"text","text":", which is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"simple, returns "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"(inserted:memberAfterInsert:)"},{"type":"text","text":", the multigraphs return the new position, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a wrapper that rejects edges returns an optional. So generic code inserts an edge by key, with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_insertEdge(fromKey:toKey:)"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The hooks are underscored because they are for wrappers inside the library: callers use the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"representations’ own ","type":"text"},{"code":"insert","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"remove","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" members, which take vertices.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"references":{"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/MutableDirectedGraph/insert(_:)":{"url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/mutabledirectedgraph\/insert(_:)","title":"insert(_:)","kind":"symbol","required":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph\/insert(_:)","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"insert"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Vertex","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P6VertexQa"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> (inserted"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Bool","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb"},{"kind":"text","text":", memberAfterInsert"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Vertex","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P6VertexQa"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Inserts "},{"code":"vertex","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" with no edges, if it is not already a vertex."}]},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/BidirectionalDirectedGraph":{"title":"BidirectionalDirectedGraph","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/BidirectionalDirectedGraph","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/bidirectionaldirectedgraph","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A directed graph that also answers in-neighborhoods: Boost’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BidirectionalGraph"},{"type":"text","text":". Kept apart"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"from "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DirectedGraph"},{"type":"text","text":" because in-adjacency usually costs extra storage, and many algorithms only"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"go forward."}],"role":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"BidirectionalDirectedGraph","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"BidirectionalDirectedGraph","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/MutableDirectedGraph/init()":{"type":"topic","title":"init()","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/mutabledirectedgraph\/init()","required":true,"fragments":[{"text":"init","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"()","kind":"text"}],"abstract":[{"text":"The empty graph.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph\/init()","kind":"symbol"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/MutableDirectedGraph/remov